WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.640
One tall figure stands in a pool of light.

2
00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:06.160
Voices drift in from the dark.

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.400
Some shout at him in the night.

4
00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:10.340
One is meant as praise.

5
00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:12.930
And one comes from his own mouth.

6
00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:18.490
Then the stage fades
into years: 1604, 1693,

7
00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:24.480
1825, 1904, 1964, 1999.

8
00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:27.850
Some mark performances, some readers.

9
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.640
So does the play question
the racism it shows,

10
00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.080
or repeat it?

11
00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:36.930
In this mission, you'll see what Venice,
Cyprus and the word Moor meant around

12
00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:38.520
1604.

13
00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:41.920
You'll track who speaks the
language of race, and when.

14
00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:45.400
And you'll follow four
centuries of critics and actors,

15
00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:51.300
from a mocking critic in 1693
to an actor's question in 1999.

16
00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:54.940
Your mission: decide whether
the play questions racism,

17
00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:56.120
or repeats it.
